## DEPED CLASS RECORD, SUBJECT TEACHER GRADING, CLASS ADVISER CONSOLIDATION, AND SCHOOL FORM 9 (SF9) REPORT CARD

### Existing School District Monitoring System — Department of Education, Philippines

## 1\. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Enhance the existing School District Monitoring System by implementing a complete, integrated, DepEd-aligned Learner Class Record and Report Card Management System.

The system must manage the complete workflow from subject-level assessment and grading to the preparation, verification, consolidation, and printing of each learner's official-style School Form 9 (SF9), commonly known as the learner's report card or Form 138.

The system must connect three main processes:

1. **Subject Teacher Class Record Management** — Each subject teacher maintains the class record for every assigned subject and class section.
2. **Grade Submission and Class Adviser Consolidation** — Subject teachers submit verified quarterly grades for their learners to the corresponding class adviser.
3. **Learner Report Card Generation (SF9)** — The class adviser consolidates the learner's grades across all applicable learning areas and grading periods into the appropriate SF9 report card.

The system must operate within the existing School District Monitoring System. Do not create a separate application, duplicate learner accounts, or replace existing school, enrollment, user management, or permission modules.

The completed feature must be fully functional, database-connected, secure, auditable, and suitable for actual school operations.

