## 3\. SYSTEM ORGANIZATION AND DATA RELATIONSHIPS

Implement a structured relationship among schools, school years, teachers, learners, sections, subjects, class records, grading periods, grade submissions, advisers, and report cards.

The logical structure should be:

School → School Year → Curriculum → Grade Level → Class Section → Enrolled Learners → Subject Assignments → Subject Teacher Class Records → Assessments and Raw Scores → Computed Quarterly Grades → Verified Grade Submissions → Class Adviser Grade Consolidation → Learner SF9 Report Card → Review, Release, and Printing

Each class record must be associated with the appropriate school, school year, grade level, section, learning area, assigned subject teacher, grading policy, and grading period.

Each learner's SF9 must be associated with the correct learner, school year, grade level, section, class adviser, and applicable report card template.

Preserve the distinction between raw assessment scores, computed grades, submitted grades, consolidated grades, and finalized report card data.

Do not calculate or consolidate grades using an unrelated class section, subject assignment, school year, or curriculum.

