## 7\. SF9 / FORM 138 LEARNER REPORT CARD MODULE

Create a complete report card module that generates the applicable official DepEd SF9 Learner's Progress Report Card from verified subject teacher submissions.

Use the official SF9 template applicable to the selected curriculum, grade level, and school year.

Do not create a generic report card and label it official SF9 unless it faithfully follows the applicable official template.

### A. Report card identity and school information

Populate the applicable fields from the existing system and verified school records, such as:

- School name.
- School ID, where applicable.
- District and Schools Division Office.
- Region, where required.
- School year.
- Learner's full name.
- Learner's prescribed identification fields.
- Grade level.
- Section.
- Curriculum or program.
- Class adviser.
- Other information explicitly required by the applicable official form.

Do not require teachers or advisers to manually encode information already available in the database.

Do not invent missing learner data.

### B. Learning areas and grades

Display all applicable learning areas in the order required by the relevant SF9 template.

For each learning area, include the required grading-period columns and final grade fields where applicable.

For templates that use four quarters, display the appropriate first-, second-, third-, and fourth-quarter grades.

The report card must also support other verified grading structures where applicable.

Each grade must originate from the appropriate accepted subject teacher submission.

Do not derive grades from unverified drafts or incomplete class records.

### C. General averages and summaries

Compute the general average and other grade summaries only according to the applicable official policy.

Follow the prescribed rules concerning:

- Included learning areas.
- Exempted or non-applicable subjects.
- Required decimal precision.
- Rounding.
- Final grade calculation.
- Promotion or retention remarks.
- Completion requirements.

Do not calculate an average by blindly including every displayed field.

Do not assume that all grades can be averaged using a simple arithmetic mean.

Where the official form requires a general average, compute it using the prescribed methodology and display the required precision.

### D. Learner progress and attendance

Include the progress, attendance, and other required reporting sections of the applicable SF9 template.

Attendance information must come from the designated authoritative attendance module or another approved data source.

Do not invent attendance entries or derive them from grade submissions.

Where attendance or another required field is unavailable, clearly indicate that the information is incomplete and follow the applicable school workflow.

### E. Remarks and promotion status

Populate remarks, promotion status, completion status, and related fields only when the applicable rules and required source data support the result.

Do not automatically mark a learner as promoted, retained, or completed based solely on a general average if additional policy conditions apply.

Provide an appropriate validation process before finalization.

### F. Report card preview

Create an on-screen report card preview that resembles the official document.

Support:

- Individual learner report cards.
- Report cards for all learners in an assigned section.
- Preview before finalization.
- Review of missing grades.
- Review of attendance and required information.
- Authorized correction and regeneration.
- Finalized historical copies.

