## 8\. REPORT CARD VALIDATION AND FINALIZATION

Before the adviser finalizes an SF9, validate the complete record.

Check:

1. All required subject grades have been received.
2. All required subject submissions have reached the required acceptance status.
3. No duplicate or incorrectly mapped learning areas exist.
4. All required grading periods are complete.
5. The report card uses the correct official template.
6. Required learner and school information is available.
7. General averages and final grades are computed correctly.
8. Attendance and required remarks are complete where applicable.
9. Promotion or completion rules have been applied correctly.
10. No unresolved correction requests remain.

Display specific validation errors instead of simply refusing to generate the report card.

Allow the adviser to save an incomplete draft for review if school policy permits, but do not label it final or released.

After finalization, freeze the applicable report card snapshot so later changes to the class roster, assessment scores, or school configuration do not silently alter the historical report card.

If a correction is necessary after finalization, require an authorized amendment or reopening process, preserve the previous version, and record the reason and responsible user.

